From: Senemos Maintainers <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: match the read completion V2 wire layout

AudioReach rd_sh_mem_ep_api.h at b38cb85a1a2543aa28aa1b27f4c380cafa5024bb
defines a 56-byte DATA_CMD_RSP_RD_SH_MEM_EP_DATA_BUFFER_DONE_V2 without
an offset field. Uke reports four successful 56-byte completions, which
the existing 60-byte size guard rejects before notifying ALSA.

Remove the extra V2 offset and its synthetic-offset bounds check. Retain
the full reply-size, status, token, address and data-size validation.
The V1 layout and all playback handling remain unchanged.

Protocol: AudioReach/audioreach-engine, fwk/api/modules/rd_sh_mem_ep_api.h,
Qualcomm Technologies, BSD-3-Clause. Linux code retains its GPL license.

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.h
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/audioreach.h
@@ -378,10 +378,9 @@
 struct data_cmd_rsp_rd_sh_mem_ep_data_buffer_done_v2 {
 	uint32_t status;
 	uint32_t buf_addr_lsw;
 	uint32_t buf_addr_msw;
 	uint32_t mem_map_handle;
 	uint32_t data_size;
-	uint32_t offset;
 	uint32_t timestamp_lsw;
 	uint32_t timestamp_msw;
 	uint32_t flags;
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm.c
@@ -683,4 +683,3 @@
 		if (hdr->token >= graph->tx_data.num_periods ||
-		    rd_done->offset > graph->tx_data.buf[hdr->token].size ||
-		    rd_done->data_size > graph->tx_data.buf[hdr->token].size - rd_done->offset) {
+		    rd_done->data_size > graph->tx_data.buf[hdr->token].size) {
 			mutex_unlock(&graph->lock);
